<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Status-bar small icon for the foreground service notification.

  Replaces android.R.drawable.stat_sys_headset (a generic system framework icon).

  Important: Android renders small icons as a SILHOUETTE — it uses only the alpha
  channel and tints the result, discarding all colour. It must therefore be a
  solid single-colour shape with no fine detail, because anything subtle turns to
  mush at ~24dp. The full traced bud pair (ic_launcher_foreground) is far too
  detailed to read at status-bar size, so this is a deliberately simplified bud.

  GEOMETRY NOTES
  The previous revision drew the head as a circle of radius 4 centred at (12, 2.4).
  Its top reached y = -1.6, i.e. OUTSIDE the 24x24 viewport, so the vector
  clipped the head's top tip. That was the cropping visible in the shade; it was
  not a centering problem.

  This revision keeps all strokes inside the viewport with margin to spare:
      head circle : centre (12, 6.2), r = 4.0  -> y 2.2 -> 10.2, x 8.0 -> 16.0
      stem        : y 10.0 -> 16.6 + 2.6 round tip, half-width 2.6
      stroke width 1.6 -> outermost ink y 1.4 -> 20.6, x 7.2 -> 16.8
  Ink centre is (12.0, 11.0); the viewport centre is (12, 12). The 1-unit rise is
  deliberate: an arc's visual mass sits below its topmost point, so centring the
  raw ink box reads as slightly low. Nothing reaches the viewport edge, so no
  clipping is possible.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <!-- Head: closed circle, drawn as two arcs so it stays inside the viewport. -->
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M8,6.2a4,4 0 1,0 8,0a4,4 0 1,0 -8,0" />

    <!-- Stem: falls from the head and rounds off at the tip. -->
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.6"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:pathData="M9.4,10L9.4,16.6a2.6,2.6 0 0,0 5.2,0L14.6,10" />
</vector>
